SUMMARY:Disney's Frozen in Concert
DESCRIPTION:Jacobs Live at the Movies returns as the IU Philharmonic Orch
 estra will present Walt Disney Animation Studios' Frozen in Concert with 
 composer Christophe Beck's GRAMMY®-nominated score performed live to the
  film. The concert will be led by conductor Ernest Richardson.  &#160\;  
 The film and its multi-Platinum soundtrack feature eight songs written by
  Academy Award®\, Emmy®\, and GRAMMY®-winning songwriters Kristen Ande
 rson-Lopez and Robert Lopez\, including the Oscar® and GRAMMY®-winning 
 song "Let It Go" performed by Idina Menzel.  &#160\;  Fearless optimist\,
  Princess Anna\, sets off on an epic journey—teaming up with rugged mou
 ntain man\, Kristoff\, and his loyal reindeer Sven—to find her sister E
 lsa\, whose icy powers have trapped the kingdom of Arendelle in eternal w
 inter. Encountering Everest-like conditions\, mystical trolls\, and a hil
 arious snowman named Olaf\, Anna and Kristoff battle the elements in a ra
 ce to save the kingdom. Voices include Kristen Bell (Anna)\, Jonathan Gro
 ff (Kristoff)\, Idina Menzel (Elsa)\, Josh Gad (Olaf)\, Santino Fontana (
 Hans)\, Alan Tudyk (Duke of Weselton). The film received the Academy® Aw
 ard for Best Animated Feature.  &#160\;  Presentation licensed by Disney 
 Concerts. All rights reserved.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><i>Jacobs Live at the Movies</i> returns 
 as the IU Philharmonic Orchestra will present Walt Disney Animation Studi
 os' <i>Frozen in Concert</i> with composer Christophe Beck's GRAMMY®-nom
 inated score performed live to the film. The concert will be led by condu
 ctor Ernest Richardson.</p><p>  &#160\;</p><p>  The film and its multi-Pl
 atinum soundtrack feature eight songs written by Academy Award®\, Emmy®
 \, and GRAMMY®-winning songwriters Kristen Anderson-Lopez and Robert Lop
 ez\, including the Oscar® and GRAMMY®-winning song "Let It Go" performe
 d by Idina Menzel.</p><p>  &#160\;</p><p>  Fearless optimist\, Princess A
 nna\, sets off on an epic journey—teaming up with rugged mountain man\,
  Kristoff\, and his loyal reindeer Sven—to find her sister Elsa\, whose
  icy powers have trapped the kingdom of Arendelle in eternal winter. Enco
 untering Everest-like conditions\, mystical trolls\, and a hilarious snow
 man named Olaf\, Anna and Kristoff battle the elements in a race to save 
 the kingdom. Voices include Kristen Bell (Anna)\, Jonathan Groff (Kristof
 f)\, Idina Menzel (Elsa)\, Josh Gad (Olaf)\, Santino Fontana (Hans)\, Ala
 n Tudyk (Duke of Weselton). The film received the Academy® Award for Bes
 t Animated Feature.</p><p>  &#160\;</p><p>  Presentation licensed by Disn
 ey Concerts. All rights reserved.</p>
